WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.129 --> 00:00:04.560
Do you ever go to the gym and there's this
one person who's there all the time at the

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:05.560
gym?

00:00:05.560 --> 00:00:08.140
Same place you've been going to, you see this
person working out so hard.

00:00:08.140 --> 00:00:11.100
It's almost as if every time you go to the
gym, they're there.

00:00:11.100 --> 00:00:13.099
But you don't see any progress with their
body.

00:00:13.099 --> 00:00:14.269
How is that even possible?

00:00:14.269 --> 00:00:15.769
See, the same goes with business.

00:00:15.769 --> 00:00:17.810
In business you have two different people.

00:00:17.810 --> 00:00:21.249
Let's just say we have Bobby, and we have
Joey.

00:00:21.249 --> 00:00:22.400
Okay?

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.340
Bobby and Joey both became an entrepreneur
at the same exact time.

00:00:25.340 --> 00:00:27.000
Same exact time.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:28.819
They're both willing to work 80 hours a week.

00:00:28.819 --> 00:00:29.819
They're all-the-timers.

00:00:29.819 --> 00:00:31.609
They're willing to work 80 hours a week.

00:00:31.609 --> 00:00:36.730
But two years later, three years later, five
years later, Bobby's business does $5 million

00:00:36.730 --> 00:00:40.120
a year, Joey's business only does a couple
hundred thousand dollars per year.

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:41.120
Why is that?

00:00:41.120 --> 00:00:42.120
Right?

00:00:42.120 --> 00:00:43.620
How is that even possible?

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:46.360
And Joey is going crazy thinking, what is
Bobby doing?

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:47.830
Did he get lucky?

00:00:47.830 --> 00:00:48.830
Nope.

00:00:48.830 --> 00:00:54.140
Bobby knew how to prioritize his time, and
Bobby gets credit for putting a better strategy

00:00:54.140 --> 00:00:57.670
in place while working very hard.

00:00:57.670 --> 00:01:02.540
So I'm going to explain to you today the strategy
quadrant and my outcome today, this video

00:01:02.540 --> 00:01:04.150
is not for everybody.

00:01:04.150 --> 00:01:06.869
So, this video's not for somebody who's a
part-timer.

00:01:06.869 --> 00:01:12.240
This video is for somebody who's minimum,
minimum working 60 hours and up and is wanting

00:01:12.240 --> 00:01:17.100
to take their business from doing a million
dollars a year to two, four, 10, 20 million

00:01:17.100 --> 00:01:18.710
dollar a year business.

00:01:18.710 --> 00:01:19.710
You're not looking at doing something small.

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.799
You want to exponentially grow your business.

00:01:21.799 --> 00:01:25.390
So now, you have four things.

00:01:25.390 --> 00:01:28.999
Entrepreneurs sometimes say, "Pat, I feel
like I'm doing so many different things.

00:01:28.999 --> 00:01:36.450
A veteran, an expert entrepreneur will rarely
say, "I'm being very overwhelmed."

00:01:36.450 --> 00:01:39.570
You rarely hear somebody who knows what they're
doing, they're overwhelmed.

00:01:39.570 --> 00:01:41.840
Typically amateurs say, "I'm very overwhelmed."

00:01:41.840 --> 00:01:45.800
I feel like I have to do this, and I'm doing
that and doing this and doing this, man, this

00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:46.800
is just too much.

00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:47.909
I don't know if I can do this."

00:01:47.909 --> 00:01:48.909
Right?

00:01:48.909 --> 00:01:49.909
Okay.

00:01:49.909 --> 00:01:50.909
Great.

00:01:50.909 --> 00:01:52.340
You're really doing four things as a CEO and
an entrepreneur.

00:01:52.340 --> 00:01:53.799
It's four things you're really doing.

00:01:53.799 --> 00:01:58.619
You're either working on your next innovative
campaign, you're either developing leaders,

00:01:58.619 --> 00:02:02.389
you're either making your operating system
better, or you're doing biz dev and sales.

00:02:02.389 --> 00:02:03.539
Very simple.

00:02:03.539 --> 00:02:07.689
One thing to keep in mind, any time you spend
time here on the bottom, this is linear, which

00:02:07.689 --> 00:02:09.340
means you're business doesn't explode.

00:02:09.340 --> 00:02:10.600
It's linear.

00:02:10.600 --> 00:02:15.440
This is like somebody who has a liquor store
or a restaurant and they make burgers or they

00:02:15.440 --> 00:02:20.820
sell beer, and every year they gross $600,000
a year.

00:02:20.820 --> 00:02:22.020
They gross a million a year.

00:02:22.020 --> 00:02:24.140
They gross $300,000 a year.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:25.170
And they're happy with that.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:27.110
That's what they're grossing every single
year.

00:02:27.110 --> 00:02:31.800
And it's been the same for 10 years, because
their main focus is here [biz dev], so it's

00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:32.800
linear.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:33.800
It hasn't exploded.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:34.800
Right?

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:39.570
And over here [top], you've got the exponential
side, when you focus on next innovative campaign

00:02:39.570 --> 00:02:41.060
and leadership development.

00:02:41.060 --> 00:02:45.700
Now, before I go into this, and dive into
this with you, I want you to understand.

00:02:45.700 --> 00:02:49.540
What you do also has to do with when you do
it.

00:02:49.540 --> 00:02:52.980
For instance, every business goes through
a different phase.

00:02:52.980 --> 00:02:54.590
Four phases they go through.

00:02:54.590 --> 00:02:58.100
One is the survival, which say it's the beginning
of the business, at any point it can go out

00:02:58.100 --> 00:02:59.100
of business.

00:02:59.100 --> 00:03:00.100
This is startup phase.

00:03:00.100 --> 00:03:05.100
The other one is formulation; you're putting
the pieces together, because you're preparing

00:03:05.100 --> 00:03:06.100
for what?

00:03:06.100 --> 00:03:07.680
An explosion.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:11.840
And then when you have an explosion at the
end, most companies, almost every one of them,

00:03:11.840 --> 00:03:15.060
if not every one of them, you will hit a plateau.

00:03:15.060 --> 00:03:16.060
Right?

00:03:16.060 --> 00:03:17.070
You will hit a plateau.

00:03:17.070 --> 00:03:21.970
But it's very important for you to be prepared
for this explosion that's going to take place.

00:03:21.970 --> 00:03:23.620
And how do you maximize that explosion?

00:03:23.620 --> 00:03:27.430
So now, with that being said, let's talk about
what these four things are that you'll be

00:03:27.430 --> 00:03:30.350
doing as an entrepreneur.

00:03:30.350 --> 00:03:31.940
First one, next innovative campaign.

00:03:31.940 --> 00:03:32.970
This is very simple.

00:03:32.970 --> 00:03:35.070
Let me explain to you what I mean by this.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.790
Right now it's holiday season.

00:03:36.790 --> 00:03:37.820
Okay?

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:40.620
Christmas is around the corner, New Year's
is coming.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:49.520
Everybody, by January 1st, is going to be
judged on the type of campaign they ran during

00:03:49.520 --> 00:03:50.750
this season.

00:03:50.750 --> 00:03:51.880
Everybody.

00:03:51.880 --> 00:03:55.580
They're going to get judged on what type of
a campaign they run during this season.

00:03:55.580 --> 00:03:58.850
There is dealerships that have to hit their
numbers by the end of the year, so you'll

00:03:58.850 --> 00:04:03.930
hear a lot of creative innovative campaigns
saying, "you know, if you buy a brand new

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:08.990
Hyundai, the next 60 days, we're going to
pay for your gas the next two years."

00:04:08.990 --> 00:04:10.030
Oh, wow.

00:04:10.030 --> 00:04:14.030
Honey, we can buy a car and they're going
to pay for two years of our gas.

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:17.420
What they're really saying is instead of selling
you the car for 28 grand, they'll sell it

00:04:17.420 --> 00:04:19.040
to you for 24 grand.

00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:20.750
And that $4,000 is two years of gas.

00:04:20.750 --> 00:04:23.720
But it's an innovative campaign, to get you
to come in.

00:04:23.720 --> 00:04:27.590
You know, Wal-Mart may say, you know, during
the holiday season we have a sale on these

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:28.590
three products.

00:04:28.590 --> 00:04:30.010
Why those three products?

00:04:30.010 --> 00:04:31.600
Because they're the most popular selling products.

00:04:31.600 --> 00:04:34.139
That brings us in, then we buy a bunch of
other things.

00:04:34.139 --> 00:04:36.560
That's their innovative campaign.

00:04:36.560 --> 00:04:38.810
Everybody gets judged on this.

00:04:38.810 --> 00:04:45.910
Unfortunately, even as a real estate agent,
or financial adviser, insurance, Fintech,

00:04:45.910 --> 00:04:52.130
whatever business you're in, every business
has a next innovative campaign.

00:04:52.130 --> 00:04:58.160
And those who don't have constant next innovative
campaigns, they don't have the inevitable

00:04:58.160 --> 00:04:59.160
explosion.

00:04:59.160 --> 00:05:00.160
That's exponential.

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:02.000
Not steady linear, exponential.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:03.630
The other one is leadership development.

00:05:03.630 --> 00:05:09.100
Leadership development is, you always identify
who the next leaders you're going to build.

00:05:09.100 --> 00:05:13.400
From the moment I figured out this business,
for the longest time my business was linear,

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:17.990
the first two years, and then I said, Look,
I want to experience an explosion.

00:05:17.990 --> 00:05:21.750
I want to take my business from doing $100,000
a year to doing tens of millions of dollars

00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:22.750
per year.

00:05:22.750 --> 00:05:24.120
How do I do that?

00:05:24.120 --> 00:05:27.660
Everything came back down to leadership development.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:32.190
So you take your business, whatever you have,
and you sit there and you say who do I have

00:05:32.190 --> 00:05:36.450
at the home office that I can make into a
major leader in the company?

00:05:36.450 --> 00:05:40.400
And you make a list of your top five, top
three, whoever the people are.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:42.520
And you start assessing them.

00:05:42.520 --> 00:05:46.620
And you say, this person needs this, they're
strengths are this, their weaknesses are this.

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.630
This person responds to this, they don't respond
to this.

00:05:48.630 --> 00:05:49.630
They're very competitive.

00:05:49.630 --> 00:05:50.630
They're not competitive.

00:05:50.630 --> 00:05:51.840
They're very sensitive.

00:05:51.840 --> 00:05:53.380
You know, he's always coming up with ideas.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:54.380
Man, he's so solid.

00:05:54.380 --> 00:05:55.490
He's got poise.

00:05:55.490 --> 00:05:57.230
I like this guy.

00:05:57.230 --> 00:05:58.889
Does he believe in the company?

00:05:58.889 --> 00:06:00.300
So what can I do with him?

00:06:00.300 --> 00:06:04.110
Then you sit down and you start identifying
what things he needs to do in the next six,

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:06.150
12 months, two years.

00:06:06.150 --> 00:06:07.150
And you present it to him.

00:06:07.150 --> 00:06:08.150
Then you work on them.

00:06:08.150 --> 00:06:10.070
You challenge him or her to grow.

00:06:10.070 --> 00:06:14.600
You do the same thing with your executive
sales people, up and coming people, it doesn't

00:06:14.600 --> 00:06:15.660
matter what it is.

00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:22.710
You, as a CEO, as an entrepreneur are going
to get judged based on the types of leaders

00:06:22.710 --> 00:06:23.710
you develop.

00:06:23.710 --> 00:06:25.500
Yesterday Tom and I were in New York.

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:26.500
We were on a flight.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:30.680
We're coming back, and Tom said, we were talking
about Bill Belichick.

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:34.590
Bill Belichick, coach of New England Patriots.

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.160
And I say, "Hey, Tom, I got a question for
you."

00:06:36.160 --> 00:06:37.160
He said, "What's that?"

00:06:37.160 --> 00:06:43.130
I said "How many coaches that have worked
under Belichick have won a Super Bowl championship?

00:06:43.130 --> 00:06:44.130
They were assistant coaches.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.150
He said you know what, actually nobody.

00:06:45.150 --> 00:06:46.150
I said, "really?"

00:06:46.150 --> 00:06:47.150
He said, "nobody."

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:51.080
I said, "That's so interesting, because you
know, Bill Walsh is known for what?

00:06:51.080 --> 00:06:56.060
Bill Walsh was known for having produced the
most people who went on and won championships

00:06:56.060 --> 00:07:00.750
for themselves, because Bill Walsh is a phenomenal
developer of leaders.

00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:05.520
Now Bill Belichick is phenomenal at building
players into leaders.

00:07:05.520 --> 00:07:06.520
Not coaches, but players.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:07.520
That was his strength.

00:07:07.520 --> 00:07:10.180
So if you're a player playing for him, you're
going to win.

00:07:10.180 --> 00:07:12.370
But coaches was a different story, right?

00:07:12.370 --> 00:07:16.150
You're going to get judged based on how well
of a job you do with leadership development.

00:07:16.150 --> 00:07:17.660
Because this is exponential.

00:07:17.660 --> 00:07:22.060
A part of this could be as you looking at
next people to recruit to bring to your company

00:07:22.060 --> 00:07:23.510
that certain talent.

00:07:23.510 --> 00:07:25.490
Then the linear side is operating systems
and biz dev.

00:07:25.490 --> 00:07:27.910
Let me explain operating systems.

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:31.220
Operating system, to most people who are watching
this, if you're an A-type personality or you're

00:07:31.220 --> 00:07:35.370
a marketer or sales CEO type of a personality,
this is boring.

00:07:35.370 --> 00:07:37.590
There's nothing exciting about operating system.

00:07:37.590 --> 00:07:41.930
But let me take a shot at trying to excite
you here, why operating system may be something

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:43.919
you ought to pay very close attention to.

00:07:43.919 --> 00:07:47.190
There are two reasons why a company goes out
of business.

00:07:47.190 --> 00:07:49.389
One, they grow too slow.

00:07:49.389 --> 00:07:51.050
Two, they grow too fast.

00:07:51.050 --> 00:07:54.830
And you know why a company goes out of business
when they grow too fast?

00:07:54.830 --> 00:07:59.850
Because they had a founder and a CEO that
had no desire to pay attention to their operating

00:07:59.850 --> 00:08:00.900
system.

00:08:00.900 --> 00:08:05.750
Because while they can handle 50, 100 sales
a month, 200 sales a month, all of a sudden,

00:08:05.750 --> 00:08:11.030
business takes off and the 200 sales a month
goes to four, 800, 1600 sales a month.

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:12.930
And the home office can't handle it no more.

00:08:12.930 --> 00:08:14.050
And everybody's backed up.

00:08:14.050 --> 00:08:15.970
And then people get complaints.

00:08:15.970 --> 00:08:17.570
Then no one wants to buy again.

00:08:17.570 --> 00:08:21.720
Then there's rumors that you become the next
eToys, where you can't deliver on your products

00:08:21.720 --> 00:08:23.500
and deliver the toys on time.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:27.720
And toys that were ordered to ship out before
Christmas don't show up until January 16,

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:28.729
then you go out of business.

00:08:28.729 --> 00:08:29.729
why?

00:08:29.729 --> 00:08:32.329
Because you did not pay attention to the operating
system.

00:08:32.329 --> 00:08:35.210
This you want to get it to the point with
your business that eventually it's simply

00:08:35.210 --> 00:08:36.360
a knob.

00:08:36.360 --> 00:08:37.710
All it is is a knob.

00:08:37.710 --> 00:08:40.660
Your system is so well defined, that you just
need to control the knob.

00:08:40.660 --> 00:08:42.060
Boom, we just need to hire three more.

00:08:42.060 --> 00:08:44.470
We can hire and afford 700 sales a month.

00:08:44.470 --> 00:08:45.470
Oh!

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:47.080
It's an increase, we need to hire seven more.

00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:49.330
It's okay, we can handle 1,400 a month.

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:50.330
Oh, we need.

00:08:50.330 --> 00:08:51.330
. . it's a knob.

00:08:51.330 --> 00:08:52.960
Oh, we don't need to, let's let go of three
people.

00:08:52.960 --> 00:08:53.960
Oh, we don't need to.

00:08:53.960 --> 00:08:56.160
. . let's just hire some temp, oh, because
it's a knob.

00:08:56.160 --> 00:08:57.480
Boom, boom, boom, boom.

00:08:57.480 --> 00:08:58.480
Very simple.

00:08:58.480 --> 00:08:59.720
Operating system.

00:08:59.720 --> 00:09:01.790
Next, biz dev and sales.

00:09:01.790 --> 00:09:06.890
Biz dev and sales is new partners, how to
make your sales better, how to make your sales

00:09:06.890 --> 00:09:09.000
process better.

00:09:09.000 --> 00:09:12.890
How to build some new relationships with vendors,
with new partnerships.

00:09:12.890 --> 00:09:16.780
Your networking, annual networking events
where everybody's there from your industry

00:09:16.780 --> 00:09:18.650
and you're going out there shaking hands with
everybody.

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:22.740
We just went to one last week, which is the
annual life insurance convention.

00:09:22.740 --> 00:09:23.740
You talk to everybody.

00:09:23.740 --> 00:09:25.000
Meeting after meeting after meeting after
meeting.

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.620
Hey, what do you guys got going on?

00:09:26.620 --> 00:09:27.620
Hey what are you working on?

00:09:27.620 --> 00:09:28.620
What's going on?

00:09:28.620 --> 00:09:30.980
Relationship, relationship, relationship,
relationship.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:33.910
That's what this [biz dev] is.

00:09:33.910 --> 00:09:35.700
Linear, exponential.

00:09:35.700 --> 00:09:37.490
Linear, exponential.

00:09:37.490 --> 00:09:42.890
If you spend most of your time in the linear
part, you are not going to explode.

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:48.240
If you spend most of your time on the exponential
part, you're getting ready for a major explosion.

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:49.240
Here's the problem.

00:09:49.240 --> 00:09:50.740
Most people are always here [linear].

00:09:50.740 --> 00:09:55.670
This is why.

00:09:55.670 --> 00:10:02.050
Just because you chose to become an entrepreneur,
doesn't make you a visionary.

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:06.120
Just because you chose to become an entrepreneur,
doesn't make you a CEO.

00:10:06.120 --> 00:10:11.660
Just because you chose to become an entrepreneur,
doesn't mean you're always thinking future.

00:10:11.660 --> 00:10:15.070
You could become an entrepreneur and you're
a technician, like it talks about in the book

00:10:15.070 --> 00:10:16.190
E-Myth.

00:10:16.190 --> 00:10:19.500
You chose to become an entrepreneur and all
you want to do is, hey, we need to make the

00:10:19.500 --> 00:10:20.500
software better.

00:10:20.500 --> 00:10:26.330
I had this one guy that I worked with, 24/7,
he spends so much time on his software, until

00:10:26.330 --> 00:10:29.050
he ran out of money and he had no sales people
and he went out of business.

00:10:29.050 --> 00:10:30.700
He spent $600,000.

00:10:30.700 --> 00:10:32.770
A complete waste of time.

00:10:32.770 --> 00:10:34.371
And I said, you need sales.

00:10:34.371 --> 00:10:35.430
You need to develop your people.

00:10:35.430 --> 00:10:36.430
Spend time with sales people.

00:10:36.430 --> 00:10:37.430
But you don't understand.

00:10:37.430 --> 00:10:39.890
If I get this product done, we're going to
blow up.

00:10:39.890 --> 00:10:43.279
It has nothing to do with the product.

00:10:43.279 --> 00:10:46.540
The product is great, but if you don't have
sales, nothing happens.

00:10:46.540 --> 00:10:50.089
So you need to ask yourself this question
as you're watching this.

00:10:50.089 --> 00:10:51.950
Very simple.

00:10:51.950 --> 00:10:53.690
Survival phase?

00:10:53.690 --> 00:10:57.170
Formulation phase?

00:10:57.170 --> 00:10:58.450
Explosion phase?

00:10:58.450 --> 00:10:59.450
Plateau phase?

00:10:59.450 --> 00:11:03.890
Okay, let's set aside plateau phase, because
plateau phase is also a whole strategy you've

00:11:03.890 --> 00:11:05.550
got to put together here.

00:11:05.550 --> 00:11:06.740
Let's bring you back.

00:11:06.740 --> 00:11:11.530
What do you think is more important during
linear phase?

00:11:11.530 --> 00:11:15.520
What's up here - next innovative campaign,
leadership development?

00:11:15.520 --> 00:11:17.430
Or operating system, biz dev and sales?

00:11:17.430 --> 00:11:19.540
What do you think is more important during
survival?

00:11:19.540 --> 00:11:23.149
Without it you could go out of business.

00:11:23.149 --> 00:11:26.370
During survival, this is decent [biz dev/sales]
